    "body": "## Pull request overview\n\nThis PR updates the `vmv.v.i` vector instruction specification to avoid invalid bit-slice ranges when writing an element at the very beginning or end of the vector register, preventing ISS assertion failures.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add conditional logic to avoid constructing slices like `v[vd][-1:0]` and `v[vd][VLEN-1:VLEN]` when the modified element touches bit 0 or bit `VLEN-1`.\n- Preserve the original concatenation-based element update behavior for non-boundary elements.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/riscv/riscv-unified-db/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
